WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.900
My son Henry doesn't watch a lot of television,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.200
although he does enjoy uncle Hank's space videos.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.240
But I recently watched 12 of the most popular programs for toddlers

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.400
to understand what he might be watching

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.300
and Hank, because I remembered that you

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.000
were a big fan of the show Blue's Clues

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.900
when you were in college,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.400
I come to you today with an introduction

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.580
to contemporary children's television.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.000
So Hank, in general, watching children's television

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.500
is a dark and surreal descent into madness,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.000
where the characters on the screen talk directly to you.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.340
So for example at the end of every episode

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.000
of Dora the Explorer

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.420
she'll be like 'What was your favourite part?'

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.560
and I'll be like, 'Well the weirdest part was the part

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.600
where you and your pet jaguar went camping

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.300
with nothing, but a flashlight and some snacks.'

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.160
And then she'll say, 'I like that part too!'

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.540
and I'll be like, 'No, I didn't like it Dora, I thought it was weird.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.280
You're a toddler, you should be inside.'

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.360
Also Hank, in the world of contemporary children's television

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.200
we've apparently abandoned child labor laws

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.920
like take for example, the Dora the Explorer spin off, Diego.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.940
Diego's like a 4 year old, who's been inexplicably

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.640
promoted to some kind of park ranger

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.220
that allows him to go around the world

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.020
and save animals.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.420
Apparently there are a lot of animals

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.760
in distress, because like Wonder Pets,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.020
which is about an operatic gerbil,

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.300
he saves animals in need,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.500
as do the kids on Little Einsteins,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.020
a show about kids who fly around in a rocket

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.000
called 'Rocket.'

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.060
But of course Hank, there are also people in need,

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.620
specifically child actors, and for those child actors

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.460
we have Special Agent Oso -

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.260
an OSO-special agent panda, who travels

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.720
around the world helping child actors learn to do things

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.040
like tie their shoes.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.540
Team Umizoomi is also in the child actor assistant business

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.080
but they specialize in Math,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.900
which can be a little bit humiliating because

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.660
they'll be like, 'Hey, do you know what shape this is?'

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.980
and I'll be like, 'Mmm, octahedron?'

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.540
and they'll say, 'That's right! its a dodecahedron.'

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.180
And I will feel the shame.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.060
Hank, there are also lots of shows about kids

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.180
who go into their backyards and have

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.080
really compelling hallucinations like- The Cat in the Hat

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.020
and the Backyardigans and Phineas and Ferb -

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.020
which, by the way, is the best television program

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.120
I have ever seen for children or adults.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.800
In fact, not to brag, but I own a

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.160
Perry the Platypus Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers doll.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.920
It airs on the Disney channel, which also

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.460
contains Mickey Mouse Clubhouse.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.880
The first time I saw Mickey Mouse Clubhouse

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.880
I was like, 'This is amazing, this is a television program

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.780
with no advertisements,' and then I realised the television program

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.060
IS the advertisement. What else?

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.900
Oh yeah, there's the hot slice of crazy known as 'Yo Gabba Gabba'.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.300
Hank, I don't know what Yo Gabba Gabba is about

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.280
but, I do know that it contains more good music than MTV.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.200
Hank, if you want to hear the Shins or Weezer or Weird Al or Mos Def on TV,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.160
you HAVE to watch Yo Gabba Gabba.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.320
And then you have the wildly popular Ni Hao, Kai-Lan,

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.900
a show that I'm surprised right wing commentators

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.380
haven't gotten upset about, given how they felt about the Teletubbies.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.140
I mean Ni Hao, Kai Lan basically teaches American children the importance of

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.760
Confucian filial piety, a smattering of Mandarin Chinese words, and the very dangerous lesson

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.920
that the best way to solve your problems is by collaborating with a tiger.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.500
Whereas in America, we know that the best way to

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.440
solve our problems is by not collaborating at all.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.860
And lastly Hank, there are currently 2 different shows on television about octopuses

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.660
who inexplicably do not need water to survive.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.120
There's the charming Oswald, and the terrifying Octonauts.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.740
So the Octonauts live at the bottom of the ocean

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.320
in some kind of pressurised contraption, and their leader appears to be this monocled

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.420
octopus and then sometimes to help animals in distress, they travel around in

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.160
this anglerfish, which is awesome, except that the anglerfish has a male voice

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.480
and we all know that is a female anglerfish, because

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.680
if it were a male, it would be just a sperm-producing parasite on her side.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.400
More importantly Hank, what's up with the octopus symbol that's on their hats

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.260
and their uniforms, and their coffee mugs?

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.880
Has their monocle octopus cohort created some kind of cult of personality where they

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.040
worship him as dear leader, and why is there a children's television program

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.920
celebrating this weird, underwater cult?!

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.280
And Hank, that's not even to mention Bubble Guppies, a show in which little mermaids

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.300
and merdudes despite living underwater, are able to have campfires.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.440
No wonder our science scores are so low.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.800
So Hank, those are my conclusions from a week of watching children's TV.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.100
Don't Forget To Be Awesome

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.340
and I will see you on Friday.

